{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02775",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 3.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Hello, come in. Mind the step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.23,
      "end_seconds": 8.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Afternoon, you know, is this seat fine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 9.27,
      "end_seconds": 13.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Well, thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.25,
      "end_seconds": 21.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.7,
      "text": "Alright, good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. Start wherever you like, I'm listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 23.53,
      "end_seconds": 26.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "He's been having sneezing in spring, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.68,
      "end_seconds": 30.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.3,
      "end_seconds": 35.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Ever since... since Friday, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.53,
      "end_seconds": 39.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.49,
      "end_seconds": 47.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "Actually, it's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.44,
      "end_seconds": 55.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.91,
      "end_seconds": 59.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I'd say all the time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.93,
      "end_seconds": 63.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.26,
      "end_seconds": 71.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kinda... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.62,
      "end_seconds": 78.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "Right, take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.89,
      "end_seconds": 85.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "About a five out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.61,
      "end_seconds": 90.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "is there something that settles it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.09,
      "end_seconds": 95.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "I get some relief from antihistamine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.01,
      "end_seconds": 98.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "What brings it on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.93,
      "end_seconds": 103.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "I, I notice it more with pollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.65,
      "end_seconds": 112.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 112.49,
      "end_seconds": 119.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "tell the doctor about the other thing, um, that's what worries me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.88,
      "end_seconds": 122.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Mm, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.72,
      "end_seconds": 132.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.25,
      "end_seconds": 141.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Oh, and a runny itchy nose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.26,
      "end_seconds": 144.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "how often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.13,
      "end_seconds": 153.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "It's, It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.2,
      "end_seconds": 161.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.01,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.01,
      "end_seconds": 165.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Honestly, on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.29,
      "end_seconds": 170.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "And loss of smell, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.94,
      "end_seconds": 180.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "Sorry, you know, what was I saying, not that I've noticed, no loss of smell."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.01,
      "end_seconds": 185.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "alright, did you get fever, facial pain or wheeze?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.62,
      "end_seconds": 199.62,
      "duration_seconds": 13.0,
      "text": "No, no fever, no facial pain, no wheeze. I did have watery eyes at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.95,
      "end_seconds": 203.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "anything different when you pass water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.49,
      "end_seconds": 208.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.58,
      "end_seconds": 224.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.38,
      "end_seconds": 237.66,
      "duration_seconds": 11.28,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I gave up cigarettes last spring. I live with my elderly mother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.19,
      "end_seconds": 241.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.58,
      "end_seconds": 245.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Just my tonsils removed, as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.36,
      "end_seconds": 250.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.91,
      "end_seconds": 260.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.59,
      "text": "I'm on escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day. Levetiracetam. I take it 500 milligrams, maybe, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.98,
      "end_seconds": 266.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.17,
      "end_seconds": 274.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.22,
      "text": "No, it's at home. Febuxostat. I take it 80 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.03,
      "end_seconds": 277.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "How long has that been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.8,
      "end_seconds": 291.45,
      "duration_seconds": 12.65,
      "text": "For two years. Loratadine, 10 milligrams, once a day. Okay, so I had carbamazepine at one point, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.17,
      "end_seconds": 296.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.27,
      "end_seconds": 302.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "my cousin has psoriasis. My father has Parkinson's disease"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.86,
      "end_seconds": 309.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.05,
      "end_seconds": 323.31,
      "duration_seconds": 13.26,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.84,
      "end_seconds": 327.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.53,
      "end_seconds": 332.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "I have anxiety, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.77,
      "end_seconds": 335.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.16,
      "end_seconds": 342.73,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "I've had epilepsy for nearly five years now i have gout"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.4,
      "end_seconds": 350.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Right, so anxiety and epilepsy are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.0,
      "end_seconds": 357.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.21,
      "end_seconds": 360.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.26,
      "end_seconds": 378.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "The inside of the nose is pale and boggy with clear mucus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.07,
      "end_seconds": 381.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.83,
      "end_seconds": 387.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.34,
      "end_seconds": 440.53,
      "duration_seconds": 37.19,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, this looks most like seasonal allergic rhinitis. Let's use fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day, the season. That should help with hay fever. Shower after being outdoors and keep windows shut when pollen is high. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 441.66,
      "end_seconds": 446.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "I'll want another look if not better in a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 447.63,
      "end_seconds": 452.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "I'll book your follow-up at the front desk on your way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 454.26,
      "end_seconds": 459.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "so, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 460.61,
      "end_seconds": 471.85,
      "duration_seconds": 11.24,
      "text": "So, I take the fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day and come back if not better in a month. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 476.46,
      "end_seconds": 480.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "yes, exactly right. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 481.96,
      "end_seconds": 485.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}